,"kind":0.007751937984496124,"drift":0.007751937984496124,"pinned":0.007751937984496124,"resource":0.007751937984496124,"protects":0.007751937984496124}}},"tokenOccurrences":{"path":{"systems":1,"inventory":1,"md":1},"title":{"inventory":1},"description":{"explains":1,"how":1,"items":1,"are":1,"stacked":1,"stored":1,"and":1,"moved":1,"between":1,"containers":1,"which":1,"service":1,"api":1,"you":1,"call":1,"to":1,"change":1,"a":1,"player's":1,"inventory":1},"type":{"system":1},"tags":{"inventory":1,"items":1,"gameplay":1,"service":1},"body":{"0":1,"1":1,"64":1,"model":1,"an":1,"inventory":1,"is":1,"a":1,"fixed-size":1,"array":1,"of":1,"itemstack":1,"slots":1,"owned":1,"by":1,"container":1,"crew":1,"member":1,"airship":1,"hold":1,"or":1,"forge":1,"input":1,"tray":1,"value":1,"type":1,"holding":1,"itemid":1,"and":1,"count":1,"stacks":1,"the":1,"same":1,"id":1,"merge":1,"up":1,"to":1,"item's":1,"maxstack":1,"for":1,"ore":1,"tools":1,"empty":1,"are":1,"represented":1,"rather":1,"than":1,"null":1,"so":1,"can":1,"be":1,"serialised":1,"without":1,"special":1,"cases":1,"service":1,"api":1,"all":1,"mutations":1,"go":1,"through":1,"inventoryservice":1,"three":1,"calls":1,"you":1,"will":1,"use":1,"tryadd":1,"containerid":1,"stack":1,"tryremove":1,"move":1,"from":1,"fromslot":1,"toslot":1,"each":1,"returns":1,"result":1,"struct":1,"instead":1,"throwing":1,"because":1,"failed":1,"adds":1,"normal":1,"gameplay":1,"outcomes":1,"raises":1,"inventorychanged":1,"with":1,"affected":1,"which":1,"hud":1,"save":1,"system":1,"subscribe":1,"constraints":1,"inventories":1,"authoritative":1,"on":1,"host":1,"clients":1,"send":1,"intents":1,"receive":1,"resulting":1,"delta":1,"sync":1,"note":1,"that":1,"in":1,"did":1,"not":1,"yet":1,"carry":1,"quality":1,"seed":1,"field":1,"was":1,"added":1,"main":1,"after":1,"freeze":1,"exactly":1,"kind":1,"drift":1,"pinned":1,"resource":1,"protects":1}},"avgFieldLength":{"path":3,"title":1,"description":20,"type":1,"tags":4,"body":129},"fieldLengths":{"path":{"1":3},"title":{"1":1},"description":{"1":20},"type":{"1":1},"tags":{"1":4},"body":{"1":129}}},"docs":{"docs":{"1":{"path":"systems/inventory.md","title":"Inventory","description":"Explains how items are stacked, stored and moved between containers, and which service API you call to change a player's inventory.","type":"system","tags":"inventory items gameplay service","body":"\n## Model\n\nAn inventory is a fixed-size array of `ItemStack` slots owned by a container: a crew member, an airship hold or a forge input tray. An `ItemStack` is a value type holding an `ItemId` and a count. Stacks of the same id merge up to the item's `MaxStack` (64 for ore, 1 for tools). Empty slots are represented by `ItemStack.Empty` rather than null so the array can be serialised without special cases.\n\n## Service API\n\nAll mutations go through `InventoryService`. The three calls you will use are `TryAdd(containerId, stack)`, `TryRemove(containerId, itemId, count)` and `Move(from, fromSlot, to, toSlot)`. Each returns a result struct instead of throwing, because failed adds are normal gameplay outcomes. The service raises `InventoryChanged` with the affected container id, which the HUD and the Save System subscribe to.\n\n## Constraints\n\nInventories are authoritative on the host. Clients send intents and receive the resulting delta through the Sync Model. Note that in 1.0.0 stacks did not yet carry a quality seed; that field was added on `main` after the freeze, which is exactly the kind of drift a pinned `resource` protects you from.\n"}},"count":1},"sorting":{"language":"english","sortableProperties":["path","title","description","type","tags","body"],"sortablePropertiesWithTypes":{"path":"string","title":"string","description":"string","type":"string","tags":"string","body":"string"},"sorts":{"path":{"docs":{"1":0},"orderedDocs":[[1,"systems/inventory.md"]],"type":"string"},"title":{"docs":{"1":0},"orderedDocs":[[1,"Inventory"]],"type":"string"},"description":{"docs":{"1":0},"orderedDocs":[[1,"Explains how items are stacked, stored and moved between containers, and which service API you call to change a player's inventory."]],"type":"string"},"type":{"docs":{"1":0},"orderedDocs":[[1,"system"]],"type":"string"},"tags":{"docs":{"1":0},"orderedDocs":[[1,"inventory items gameplay service"]],"type":"string"},"body":{"docs":{"1":0},"orderedDocs":[[1,"\n## Model\n\nAn inventory is a fixed-size array of `ItemStack` slots owned by a container: a crew member, an airship hold or a forge input tray. An `ItemStack` is a value type holding an `ItemId` and a count. Stacks of the same id merge up to the item's `MaxStack` (64 for ore, 1 for tools). Empty slots are represented by `ItemStack.Empty` rather than null so the array can be serialised without special cases.\n\n## Service API\n\nAll mutations go through `InventoryService`. The three calls you will use are `TryAdd(containerId, stack)`, `TryRemove(containerId, itemId, count)` and `Move(from, fromSlot, to, toSlot)`. Each returns a result struct instead of throwing, because failed adds are normal gameplay outcomes. The service raises `InventoryChanged` with the affected container id, which the HUD and the Save System subscribe to.\n\n## Constraints\n\nInventories are authoritative on the host. Clients send intents and receive the resulting delta through the Sync Model. Note that in 1.0.0 stacks did not yet carry a quality seed; that field was added on `main` after the freeze, which is exactly the kind of drift a pinned `resource` protects you from.\n"]],"type":"string"}},"enabled":true,"isSorted":true},"pinning":{"rules":[]},"language":"english"}